From: NumberOneGit rpi5-uefi contributors
Date: Sun, 17 Aug 2026 13:00:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Platform/RaspberryPi, Silicon/Broadcom: RPi5 port (changed files)

The NumberOneGit/edk2-platforms fork's RPi5 port, reduced to its
modifications and deletions of files that exist upstream at the fork's
merge-base (80ee8b861, 2024-03-12). The fork's ADDED files ship separately
as meta-rpi5-uefi/.../files/edk2-platforms-rpi5/, copied into the tree by
the recipe's do_patch:prepend BEFORE this and the later patches apply.

Scope is limited to the package trees this build actually compiles
(Platform/RaspberryPi, Silicon/Broadcom, Silicon/RaspberryPi). The fork's
one bulk-sync commit ("Nov 29 update") also touched 187 files in other
vendors' platform trees to chase newer-edk2 API churn; none of those are
referenced by RPi5.dsc/.fdf and they are deliberately dropped.

Includes the fork's deletion of Platform/RaspberryPi/Library/ResetLib
(replaced by PSCI reset paths).

Generated from NumberOneGit/edk2-platforms 4e426104a with:
  git diff --diff-filter=MD 80ee8b861 4e426104a -- \
    Platform/RaspberryPi Silicon/Broadcom Silicon/RaspberryPi

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [platform port carried out-of-tree]
---
